 ],
 "answer_text": "Found 3 gene records for cystic fibrosis: CF transmembrane conductance regulator [1], Fc gamma receptor IIa [2] and transforming growth factor beta 1 [3], linked to 1 disease: Cystic fibrosis [12]. \n\nThe gene associated with cystic fibrosis in the knowledge graph is NCBIGene:1080, named CF transmembrane conductance regulator [1]. Two additional genes\u2014NCBIGene:2212 (Fc gamma receptor IIa) [2] and NCBIGene:7040 (transforming growth factor beta 1) [3]. \n\nAdditional Associated Genes\n\nNCBIGene:2212, named Fc gamma receptor IIa [2], and NCBIGene:7040, named transforming growth factor beta 1 [3]. \n\nClinical Features and Literature\n\nMedGen lists these clinical features: Asthma [4], Bronchiectasis [5], Clubbing of fingers [6], Dehydration [7], Diarrhea [8], Hemoptysis [9], Hepatomegaly [10] and Hepatosplenomegaly [11]. \n\nDisease records found\n\nDisease name: Cystic fibrosis [12]. \n\nGene-to-disease mapping\n\nGene NCBIGene:1080, name: CF transmembrane conductance regulator [1]. Gene NCBIGene:2212, name: Fc gamma receptor IIa [2]. Gene NCBIGene:7040, name: transforming growth factor beta 1 [3]. \n\nPubmed records found\n\nPubmed title: Encephalopathy in cystic fibrosis [13]. Pubmed title: 3.22 Nutrition in Cystic Fibrosis [40]. Pubmed title: Editorial: Cystic Fibrosis in Children [42]. Pubmed title: Azithromycin and cystic fibrosis [44]. Pubmed title: Editorial: Cystic fibrosis-related diabetes [46]. \n\nMedgen records found\n\nMedgen title: Cystic fibrosis [14]. \n\nClinical features MedGen lists for Cystic fibrosis\n\nMedgen clinical_features: Asthma [4]. Medgen clinical_features: Bronchiectasis [5]. Medgen clinical_features: Clubbing of fingers [6]. Medgen clinical_features: Dehydration [7]. Medgen clinical_features: Diarrhea [8]. Medgen clinical_features: Hemoptysis [9]. Medgen clinical_features: Hepatomegaly [10]. Medgen clinical_features: Hepatosplenomegaly [11]. Medgen clinical_features: Hypercalciuria [15]. Medgen clinical_features: Male infertility [16]. Medgen clinical_features: Cirrhosis of liver [17]. Medgen clinical_features: Biliary cirrhosis [18]. Medgen clinical_features: Nasal polyposis [19]. Medgen clinical_features: Pancreatitis [20]. Medgen clinical_features: Cor pulmonale [21]. Medgen clinical_features: Rectal prolapse [22]. Medgen clinical_features: Steatorrhea [23]. Medgen clinical_features: Chronic sinusitis [24]. Medgen clinical_features: Exocrine pancreatic insufficiency [25]. Medgen clinical_features: Recurrent pneumonia [26]. Medgen clinical_features: Chronic lung disease [27]. Medgen clinical_features: Ileus [28]. Medgen clinical_features: Reduced forced vital capacity [29]. Medgen clinical_features: Elevated sweat chloride [30]. Medgen clinical_features: Recurrent bronchopulmonary infections [31]. Medgen clinical_features: Failure to thrive [32]. Medgen clinical_features: Meconium ileus [33]. Medgen clinical_features: Reduced forced expiratory volume in one second [34]. Medgen clinical_features: Decreased forced expiratory flow 25-75% [35]. Medgen clinical_features: Hyperpolarized transepithelial nasal potential difference [36]. Medgen clinical_features: Salty tasting skin [37]. \n\nLiterature entity records found\n\nLiterature entity name: Cystic Fibrosis [38]. \n\nClinical trial records found\n\nClinical trial name: Assessment of Quadriceps Muscle Electrostimulation Used in Patients Suffering From Cystic Fibrosis [39]. Clinical trial name: A Study of Topical Danazol for the Treatment of Pain Associated With Fibrocystic Breast Disease [41]. Clinical trial name: Efficacy and Safety of ONCOXIN in Patients With Breast Fibrocystic Disease [43]. Clinical trial name: A Clinical Study on the Efficacy and Safety of the Treatment of Hyperplasia of Mammary Glands With Xiaoru Sanjie Capsule [45]. Clinical trial name: Pregnancies and Cystic Fibrosis [47]. "
